  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROMOTING SUSTAINED GROWTH OF EASTERN BLACK RHINO (DICEROS BICORNIS MICHAELI) POPULATIONS AT OL PEJETA AND SERA CONSERVANCIES, KENYA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT IN OL PEJETA CONSERVANCY AND SERA WILDLIFE CONSERVANCY IN KENYA BY IMPROVING MONITORING, BIOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT, RESILIENT HABITAT MANAGEMENT, AND LOCAL PARTNER ENGAGEMENT TO ENSURE THE CONTINUED RECOVERY OF BLACK RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITAT. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE THE EASTERN BLACK RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING, PREDATION, HABITAT DEGRADATION AND LOSS, AND ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTY CAUSED BY DROUGHTS, THE COVID-19 PANDEMIC, AND DECLINING TOURISM. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) EQUIPPING RHINOCEROS MONITORING TEAMS (2) CONDUCTING BIOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT TO PROMOTE RHINOCEROS PRODUCTIVITY (3) ESTIMATING ECOLOGICAL CARRYING CAPACITY (4) ENSURING CONSISTENT WATER SUPPLY AND (5) ENGAGING WITH LOCAL COMMUNITY MEMBERS TO SUPPORT BLACK RHINOCEROS CONSERVATION EFFORTS.</narrative>
  </description>
